From 256306b68503e1511ae71210d61611a3b4ca175c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:23:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(relayer): H7 stored-result revalidation and dedup
 key (lifecycle Level 1)

Profile H7 (rule V6) in the relayer, behind
`user_decrypt_signature_check.profile_h.revalidate_stored_results`:

- Deduplication of user decryption requests is keyed on the signature and
  the validity window as well as the request content (`dedup_key`); today's
  key ignores both, so an equivalent request with a new signature and window
  is served the stored job.
- Before the shares of a completed job are served on GET, the host ACL is
  checked again (the same per-handle checks as the readiness check); a
  refusal answers 400 `not_allowed_on_host_acl` and serves nothing.

Also, from P0.4: two pre-check tests for an account whose code is an
ECDSA-disabled delegation indicator (EIP-7851, `0xef0101 || delegate`):
under Profile H `enforce` its root key is refused and the EIP-7702 shim does
not apply.

Tests: an integration test (tests/user_decrypt_v3_h7_test.rs) runs the
same, and an equivalent, request after retirement with and without H7; a
unit test covers the dedup key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
